@startuml
title Sequence Diagram 1: JWT Authentication and Policy Enforcement Workflow

actor "Data Analyst" as Analyst
participant "Client\n(SQL Client / Application)" as Client
participant "JWT Authentication\nService" as JWTAuth
participant "Trino\nFederated SQL Engine" as Trino
participant "OPA\nPolicy Decision Point" as OPA
participant "Project Nessie\nMetadata Catalog" as Nessie
participant "Apache Iceberg" as Iceberg
database "MinIO\nCustomer Domain" as MinIOCust
database "MinIO\nDeposits Domain" as MinIODep

== User Authentication ==

Analyst -> Client : Login(username,password)
Client -> JWTAuth : Authenticate Credentials
activate JWTAuth
JWTAuth --> Client : JWT Token\n(role, domain, expiry)
deactivate JWTAuth
Client --> Analyst : Authentication Successful

== Query Submission ==

Analyst -> Client : Execute SQL Query
activate Client
Client -> Trino : SQL Query + JWT Token
activate Trino

note right of Trino
  Extract JWT claims:
  • User Role
  • Domain
  • Permissions
  • Expiry
end note

== Policy Evaluation ==

Trino -> OPA : Evaluate Access Request\n(User Claims + SQL Query)
activate OPA

note right of OPA
  Rego Policies Evaluate:
  • RBAC (native to Trino)
end note

alt Access Allowed
    OPA --> Trino : Allow
    deactivate OPA
    Trino -> Nessie : Resolve Iceberg Metadata
    activate Nessie
    Nessie --> Trino : Table Metadata
    deactivate Nessie
    Trino -> Iceberg : Read Table Snapshot
    activate Iceberg

    alt Customer Domain
        Iceberg -> MinIOCust : Read Customer Data
        activate MinIOCust
        MinIOCust --> Iceberg : Records
        deactivate MinIOCust
    else Deposits Domain
        Iceberg -> MinIODep : Read Deposit Data
        activate MinIODep
        MinIODep --> Iceberg : Records
        deactivate MinIODep
    end

    note right of Iceberg
      No domain check here
    end note

    Iceberg --> Trino : Query Result
    deactivate Iceberg

    note right of Trino
      No masking applied here
    end note

    Trino --> Client : Full Result Set\n(plaintext PII included)
    deactivate Trino

    Client -> OPA : POST /v1/data/datamesh/masking/masked_columns
    activate OPA
    OPA --> Client : masked_columns for this role
    deactivate OPA

    Client -> Client : Redact masked_columns\n('***' substitution)

    note right of Client
      Masking applied here (app),
      not inside Trino
    end note

    Client --> Analyst : Display Response
else Access Denied
    OPA --> Trino : Deny
    deactivate OPA
    Trino --> Client : HTTP 403 Forbidden\nPolicy Violation
    deactivate Trino
    Client --> Analyst : Display Response
end

deactivate Client

== Audit Logging ==

Trino -> OPA : Record Decision Metadata

note right of OPA
  Audit Information
  • User ID
  • Role
  • Domain
  • SQL Statement
  • Policy Version
  • Decision
  • Timestamp
  • Compliance Rule
  (GDPR / BCBS239 / FCA)
end note

@enduml
